From a1434334fe2701678ad679d5baa188146a24de79 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nura G8x <nura-g8x@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 08:07:58 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] rpmsg: glink: do not unregister the rpdev from destroy_ept

When an rpmsg driver's probe fails, rpmsg_dev_probe() destroys the
endpoint it created. For GLINK that endpoint is the channel's only one,
and qcom_glink_destroy_ept() unregistered channel->rpdev, the device that
is being probed. device_del() then waits for the device lock that the
driver core holds around probe, and the probing task hangs forever. On
the LG G8x a fastrpc probe failure left udev-worker stuck in
rpmsg_dev_probe -> qcom_glink_destroy_ept -> device_del, and every later
reboot hung in device_shutdown() -> wait_for_device_probe(). The same
self-deadlock is reachable from rpmsg_dev_remove().

The rpdev stands for the channel the remote opened and is unregistered
in qcom_glink_rx_close() when the remote closes it. Only send the close
request from destroy_ept.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/drivers/rpmsg/qcom_glink_native.c b/drivers/rpmsg/qcom_glink_native.c
index 9ef17c2..fc03cb3 100644
--- a/drivers/rpmsg/qcom_glink_native.c
+++ b/drivers/rpmsg/qcom_glink_native.c
@@ -1418,9 +1418,14 @@ static void qcom_glink_destroy_ept(struct rpmsg_endpoint *ept)
 	channel->ept.cb = NULL;
 	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&channel->recv_lock, flags);
 
-	/* Decouple the potential rpdev from the channel */
-	qcom_glink_remove_rpmsg_device(glink, channel);
-
+	/*
+	 * Do not unregister channel->rpdev here. The channel's only endpoint
+	 * is the rpdev's own one, so this runs from rpmsg_dev_probe()'s error
+	 * path or rpmsg_dev_remove() with the rpdev's device lock held, and
+	 * device_del() would wait for that lock forever. The rpdev stands for
+	 * the remote's channel and is unregistered when the remote closes it
+	 * (qcom_glink_rx_close()).
+	 */
 	qcom_glink_send_close_req(glink, channel);
 }
 
